# 1. `gold.dim_customers`

## Purpose

The `gold.dim_customers` view stores customer information enriched with **demographic and geographic attributes**.

It serves as the main **Customer Dimension** in the Gold Layer and is used to analyze sales and customer behavior.

## Columns

| Column | Data Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `customer_key` | `INT` | Surrogate key uniquely identifying each customer record in the dimension. |
| `customer_id` | `INT` | Unique numerical identifier assigned to the customer. |
| `customer_number` | `NVARCHAR(50)` | Alphanumeric customer identifier used for tracking and referencing. |
| `first_name` | `NVARCHAR(50)` | Customer's first name. |
| `last_name` | `NVARCHAR(50)` | Customer's last name or family name. |
| `country` | `NVARCHAR(50)` | Customer's country of residence, such as `Australia`. |
| `marital_status` | `NVARCHAR(50)` | Customer's marital status, such as `Married` or `Single`. |
| `gender` | `NVARCHAR(50)` | Customer's gender, such as `Male`, `Female`, or `n/a`. |
| `birthdate` | `DATE` | Customer's date of birth in `YYYY-MM-DD` format. |
| `create_date` | `DATE` | Date when the customer record was created in the source system. |

